window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b345-c1802438f080fbcc.json"]={sha256:"c1802438f080fbcc8a66826a53425d0172c185ca2c855e8acc93c10a8b0c814c",value:{"id":"b345","title":"軌道扣件彈性設計","titleEn":"Resilient rail-fastening design","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"軌道扣件彈性設計以「扣件預壓彈性絕緣與疲勞的共同設計」為主線，將十個物理或系統問題拆成機制、計算、驗證與診斷。扣件同時控制鋼軌位置、提供彈性支承與維持電氣條件，增加夾持力並不保證所有性能改善；墊片、彈條與錨定件的路徑需分開辨認。每個單元附帶可重算的假想數據與敏感度，學員需提交帶單位的工作表、可區分失效的證據及模型邊界。","summaryEn":"This course develops fastener preload resilience insulation and fatigue design through ten physical or systems questions, each studied through mechanism, calculation, verification and diagnosis. Fastenings locate the rail, provide resilient support and maintain electrical conditions; increasing clamping force does not improve every property, so pads, clips and anchors need separate load-path interpretation. Every unit contains reproducible assumed inputs and a sensitivity calculation. Learners submit a worksheet with units, discriminating evidence for failures, and explicit model boundaries.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-track","subcategoryTitle":"軌道與土建工程","subcategoryTitleEn":"Track and civil engineering","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-track","learningTags":["rail","rail-track","track"],"architectureFamily":"rail-track","architectureNodes":[["鋼軌載入","Rail loading"],["彈條扣壓","Clip force"],["墊板彈性","Pad elasticity"],["錨固支承","Anchored support"],["縱向阻力","Longitudinal resistance"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-track","labels":["鋼軌載入","彈條扣壓","墊板彈性","錨固支承","縱向阻力"],"labelsEn":["Rail loading","Clip force","Pad elasticity","Anchored support","Longitudinal resistance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"以下為跨單元的原創假想工作表。先用第一單元定義邊界與單位，再以第二單元檢查另一個控制量，最後用第三單元提出前兩式未涵蓋的另一個檢查問題。原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=44 kN/mm。模型邊界：從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。只把 k1 增加百分之十，y=62.5 kN/mm。模型邊界：兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。把兩個算例的單一輸入敏感度放在同一張決策表，說明哪個變化最值得先量測；不可把不同物理量的裸數字直接比較，也不可把任一結果當成實際設備的設計、施工或營運許可。","textEn":"This original worksheet connects the first three units using assumed inputs. Establish boundaries and units with the first unit, examine another controlling quantity with the second, and use the third to pose a separate check outside the first two equations. Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 kN/mm. Boundary: Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm. Increasing only k1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=62.5 kN/mm. Boundary: Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.Put both single-input sensitivities in one decision table and explain which change most deserves measurement. Do not compare bare numbers with different physical dimensions, and do not treat any result as design approval, a construction procedure or operating permission.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b345-v16-s1","title":"墊片壓縮剛度與平行支承合成","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness & Parallel support stiffness","description":"本階段聚焦「墊片壓縮剛度」與「平行支承合成」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Pad compression stiffness\" and \"Parallel support stiffness\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b345-v16-01","title":"墊片壓縮剛度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「墊片壓縮剛度」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Pad compression stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"剛度應由指定載重區間的力位移關係定義。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 kN/mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率。使用載入卸載斜率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「墊片壓縮剛度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Stiffness should be defined over a specified loading interval. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 44 kN/mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate. Use loading and unloading slopes as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pad compression stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「墊片壓縮剛度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pad compression stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-01-k1","title":"墊片壓縮剛度","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness","text":"剛度應由指定載重區間的力位移關係定義。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 44 kN/mm。","textEn":"Stiffness should be defined over a specified loading interval. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「墊片壓縮剛度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Pad compression stiffness\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴","剛度應由指定載重區間的力位移關係定義。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad.","Stiffness should be defined over a specified loading interval.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剛度應由指定載重區間的力位移關係定義。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Stiffness should be defined over a specified loading interval. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b345-v16-02","title":"墊片壓縮剛度：定量估算","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「墊片壓縮剛度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Pad compression stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=44 kN/mm。模型邊界：從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 kN/mm. Boundary: Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以載入卸載斜率區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型分級力位移、預壓零點及卸載回復建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use loading and unloading slopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=44 kN/mm。模型邊界：從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=44 kN/mm. Boundary: Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「墊片壓縮剛度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Pad compression stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm；y=F/d=40 kN/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=60 kN, d=1.5 mm; y=F/d=40 kN/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b345-v16-03","title":"墊片壓縮剛度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「墊片壓縮剛度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Pad compression stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以載入卸載斜率區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型分級力位移、預壓零點及卸載回復建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「墊片壓縮剛度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use loading and unloading slopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model stepwise force-displacement, preload origin and unloading recovery, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Pad compression stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「墊片壓縮剛度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴造成偏離的合成觀察，以載入卸載斜率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Pad compression stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. Explain which evidence in loading and unloading slopes distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以載入卸載斜率區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型分級力位移、預壓零點及卸載回復建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「墊片壓縮剛度」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use loading and unloading slopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using low-load model stepwise force-displacement, preload origin and unloading recovery, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Pad compression stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「墊片壓縮剛度」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出從明確零點取得割線剛度；固定溫度及載入速率如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴造成偏離的合成觀察，以載入卸載斜率說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Pad compression stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Secant stiffness is measured from a defined origin at fixed temperature and loading rate. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. Explain which evidence in loading and unloading slopes distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「墊片壓縮剛度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Pad compression stiffness\"?","options":["本單元以載入卸載斜率區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型分級力位移、預壓零點及卸載回復建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓"],"optionsEn":["Use loading and unloading slopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以載入卸載斜率區分模型與觀察，先用低載模型分級力位移、預壓零點及卸載回復建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use loading and unloading slopes to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b345-v16-04","title":"墊片壓縮剛度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Pad compression stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「墊片壓縮剛度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pad compression stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴。這個失效與「墊片壓縮剛度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載入卸載斜率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. This failure and a measurement bias in Pad compression stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check loading and unloading slopes rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用載入卸載斜率作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴。這個失效與「墊片壓縮剛度」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載入卸載斜率，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. This failure and a measurement bias in Pad compression stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check loading and unloading slopes rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「墊片壓縮剛度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Pad compression stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element."],"answer":1,"explanation":"非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b345-v16-05","title":"平行支承合成：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Parallel support stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「平行支承合成」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Parallel support stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同位移的平行支承剛度相加。本模型把 k1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 62.5 kN/mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性。使用共同位移與分力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「平行支承合成」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Parallel supports sharing displacement have additive stiffness. In this model, k1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 62.5 kN/mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic. Use common displacement and force sharing as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel support stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「平行支承合成」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel support stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-05-k1","title":"平行支承合成","titleEn":"Parallel support stiffness","text":"同位移的平行支承剛度相加。本模型把 k1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 62.5 kN/mm。","textEn":"Parallel supports sharing displacement have additive stiffness. In this model, k1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「平行支承合成」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Parallel support stiffness\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度","同位移的平行支承剛度相加。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","Parallel supports sharing displacement have additive stiffness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同位移的平行支承剛度相加。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Parallel supports sharing displacement have additive stiffness. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b345-v16-06","title":"平行支承合成：定量估算","titleEn":"Parallel support stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平行支承合成」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Parallel support stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。只把 k1 增加百分之十，y=62.5 kN/mm。模型邊界：兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm. Increasing only k1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=62.5 kN/mm. Boundary: Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以共同位移與分力區分模型與觀察，先用共同位移、兩支承分力與初始間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use common displacement and force sharing to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。只把 k1 增加百分之十，y=62.5 kN/mm。模型邊界：兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm. Increasing only k1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=62.5 kN/mm. Boundary: Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「平行支承合成」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Parallel support stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm；y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=25 kN/mm, k2=35 kN/mm; y=k1+k2=60 kN/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b345-v16-07","title":"平行支承合成：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Parallel support stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平行支承合成」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Parallel support stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以共同位移與分力區分模型與觀察，先用共同位移、兩支承分力與初始間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平行支承合成」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use common displacement and force sharing to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using common displacement, separate support forces and initial gaps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Parallel support stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「平行支承合成」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件造成偏離的合成觀察，以共同位移與分力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Parallel support stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. Explain which evidence in common displacement and force sharing distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以共同位移與分力區分模型與觀察，先用共同位移、兩支承分力與初始間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「平行支承合成」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use common displacement and force sharing to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using common displacement, separate support forces and initial gaps, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Parallel support stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「平行支承合成」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩支承保持接觸且位移相同；各元件線彈性如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件造成偏離的合成觀察，以共同位移與分力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Parallel support stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Both supports stay in contact with identical displacement; each component is linearly elastic. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. Explain which evidence in common displacement and force sharing distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「平行支承合成」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Parallel support stiffness\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以共同位移與分力區分模型與觀察，先用共同位移、兩支承分力與初始間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use common displacement and force sharing to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以共同位移與分力區分模型與觀察，先用共同位移、兩支承分力與初始間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use common displacement and force sharing to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b345-v16-08","title":"平行支承合成：失效診斷","titleEn":"Parallel support stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平行支承合成」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Parallel support stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件。這個失效與「平行支承合成」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查共同位移與分力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. This failure and a measurement bias in Parallel support stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check common displacement and force sharing rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用共同位移與分力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件。這個失效與「平行支承合成」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查共同位移與分力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. This failure and a measurement bias in Parallel support stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check common displacement and force sharing rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「平行支承合成」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Parallel support stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度","支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element."],"answer":2,"explanation":"支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b345-v16-s2","title":"串聯支承合成與夾持力平均壓力","titleEn":"Series support stiffness & Clamping mean pressure","description":"本階段聚焦「串聯支承合成」與「夾持力平均壓力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Series support stiffness\" and \"Clamping mean pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b345-v16-09","title":"串聯支承合成：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Series support stiffness: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「串聯支承合成」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Series support stiffness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同力的串聯元件位移相加，因此總剛度小於各元件。本模型把 k1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 28.3871 kN/mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。兩元件承受相同力；不另有旁路支承或滑移。使用各層位移分量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「串聯支承合成」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Series elements share force and add displacement, giving a stiffness below either element. In this model, k1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 28.3871 kN/mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Both components carry the same force; no bypass support or slip is present. Use displacement in each layer as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Series support stiffness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm；y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm; y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「串聯支承合成」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Series support stiffness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-09-k1","title":"串聯支承合成","titleEn":"Series support stiffness","text":"同力的串聯元件位移相加，因此總剛度小於各元件。本模型把 k1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 28.3871 kN/mm。","textEn":"Series elements share force and add displacement, giving a stiffness below either element. In this model, k1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「串聯支承合成」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Series support stiffness\" is correct?","options":["同力的串聯元件位移相加，因此總剛度小於各元件。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中"],"optionsEn":["Series elements share force and add displacement, giving a stiffness below either element.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同力的串聯元件位移相加，因此總剛度小於各元件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Series elements share force and add displacement, giving a stiffness below either element. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b345-v16-10","title":"串聯支承合成：定量估算","titleEn":"Series support stiffness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「串聯支承合成」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Series support stiffness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm；y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm。只把 k1 增加百分之十，y=28.3871 kN/mm。模型邊界：兩元件承受相同力；不另有旁路支承或滑移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm; y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm. Increasing only k1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=28.3871 kN/mm. Boundary: Both components carry the same force; no bypass support or slip is present; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以各層位移分量區分模型與觀察，先用每層位移、共同力及總位移閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use displacement in each layer to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm；y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm。只把 k1 增加百分之十，y=28.3871 kN/mm。模型邊界：兩元件承受相同力；不另有旁路支承或滑移；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm; y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm. Increasing only k1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=28.3871 kN/mm. Boundary: Both components carry the same force; no bypass support or slip is present; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「串聯支承合成」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Series support stiffness\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm；y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm; y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm；y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k1=40 kN/mm, k2=80 kN/mm; y=k1*k2/(k1+k2)=26.6667 kN/mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b345-v16-11","title":"串聯支承合成：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Series support stiffness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「串聯支承合成」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Series support stiffness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以各層位移分量區分模型與觀察，先用每層位移、共同力及總位移閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「串聯支承合成」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use displacement in each layer to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using individual layer displacement, common force and total-displacement closure, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Series support stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「串聯支承合成」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩元件承受相同力；不另有旁路支承或滑移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以各層位移分量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Series support stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Both components carry the same force; no bypass support or slip is present. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. Explain which evidence in displacement in each layer distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以各層位移分量區分模型與觀察，先用每層位移、共同力及總位移閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「串聯支承合成」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use displacement in each layer to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using individual layer displacement, common force and total-displacement closure, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Series support stiffness. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「串聯支承合成」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出兩元件承受相同力；不另有旁路支承或滑移如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度造成偏離的合成觀察，以各層位移分量說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Series support stiffness, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Both components carry the same force; no bypass support or slip is present. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. Explain which evidence in displacement in each layer distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「串聯支承合成」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Series support stiffness\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化","本單元以各層位移分量區分模型與觀察，先用每層位移、共同力及總位移閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.","Use displacement in each layer to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以各層位移分量區分模型與觀察，先用每層位移、共同力及總位移閉合差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use displacement in each layer to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b345-v16-12","title":"串聯支承合成：失效診斷","titleEn":"Series support stiffness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「串聯支承合成」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Series support stiffness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度。這個失效與「串聯支承合成」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各層位移分量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. This failure and a measurement bias in Series support stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement in each layer rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用各層位移分量作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度。這個失效與「串聯支承合成」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查各層位移分量，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. This failure and a measurement bias in Series support stiffness can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement in each layer rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「串聯支承合成」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Series support stiffness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中"],"optionsEn":["Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b345-v16-13","title":"夾持力平均壓力：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Clamping mean pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「夾持力平均壓力」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Clamping mean pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"平均壓力描述名義接觸區，彈條接觸邊緣可更高。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 MPa。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。接觸面積與夾持合力已知；忽略局部邊緣峰值。使用接觸印跡與力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「夾持力平均壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Mean pressure describes nominal contact while clip-contact edges can carry more. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 11 MPa. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Contact area and clamp resultant are known; local edge peaks are omitted. Use contact imprint and force as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Skew installation concentrates local pressure; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Clamping mean pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2；y=F*1000/A=10 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2; y=F*1000/A=10 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「夾持力平均壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Clamping mean pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-13-k1","title":"夾持力平均壓力","titleEn":"Clamping mean pressure","text":"平均壓力描述名義接觸區，彈條接觸邊緣可更高。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 11 MPa。","textEn":"Mean pressure describes nominal contact while clip-contact edges can carry more. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「夾持力平均壓力」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Clamping mean pressure\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中","平均壓力描述名義接觸區，彈條接觸邊緣可更高。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure.","Mean pressure describes nominal contact while clip-contact edges can carry more.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均壓力描述名義接觸區，彈條接觸邊緣可更高。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Mean pressure describes nominal contact while clip-contact edges can carry more. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b345-v16-14","title":"夾持力平均壓力：定量估算","titleEn":"Clamping mean pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「夾持力平均壓力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Clamping mean pressure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2；y=F*1000/A=10 MPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=11 MPa。模型邊界：接觸面積與夾持合力已知；忽略局部邊緣峰值；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2; y=F*1000/A=10 MPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 MPa. Boundary: Contact area and clamp resultant are known; local edge peaks are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以接觸印跡與力區分模型與觀察，先用模型夾持力、壓敏印跡及偏心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use contact imprint and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2；y=F*1000/A=10 MPa。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=11 MPa。模型邊界：接觸面積與夾持合力已知；忽略局部邊緣峰值；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2; y=F*1000/A=10 MPa. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=11 MPa. Boundary: Contact area and clamp resultant are known; local edge peaks are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「夾持力平均壓力」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Clamping mean pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2；y=F*1000/A=10 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2; y=F*1000/A=10 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2；y=F*1000/A=10 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=20 kN, A=2000 mm2; y=F*1000/A=10 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b345-v16-15","title":"夾持力平均壓力：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Clamping mean pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「夾持力平均壓力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Clamping mean pressure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以接觸印跡與力區分模型與觀察，先用模型夾持力、壓敏印跡及偏心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「夾持力平均壓力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use contact imprint and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model clamp force, pressure-sensitive imprint and eccentricity, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clamping mean pressure. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「夾持力平均壓力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出接觸面積與夾持合力已知；忽略局部邊緣峰值如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中造成偏離的合成觀察，以接觸印跡與力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clamping mean pressure, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Contact area and clamp resultant are known; local edge peaks are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure. Explain which evidence in contact imprint and force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Skew installation concentrates local pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以接觸印跡與力區分模型與觀察，先用模型夾持力、壓敏印跡及偏心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「夾持力平均壓力」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use contact imprint and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model clamp force, pressure-sensitive imprint and eccentricity, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clamping mean pressure. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「夾持力平均壓力」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出接觸面積與夾持合力已知；忽略局部邊緣峰值如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中造成偏離的合成觀察，以接觸印跡與力說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clamping mean pressure, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Contact area and clamp resultant are known; local edge peaks are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure. Explain which evidence in contact imprint and force distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「夾持力平均壓力」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Clamping mean pressure\"?","options":["本單元以接觸印跡與力區分模型與觀察，先用模型夾持力、壓敏印跡及偏心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴"],"optionsEn":["Use contact imprint and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以接觸印跡與力區分模型與觀察，先用模型夾持力、壓敏印跡及偏心位置建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use contact imprint and force to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b345-v16-16","title":"夾持力平均壓力：失效診斷","titleEn":"Clamping mean pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「夾持力平均壓力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Clamping mean pressure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中。這個失效與「夾持力平均壓力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接觸印跡與力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Skew installation concentrates local pressure. This failure and a measurement bias in Clamping mean pressure can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact imprint and force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用接觸印跡與力作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Skew installation concentrates local pressure; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中。這個失效與「夾持力平均壓力」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查接觸印跡與力，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Skew installation concentrates local pressure. This failure and a measurement bias in Clamping mean pressure can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check contact imprint and force rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「夾持力平均壓力」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Clamping mean pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Skew installation concentrates local pressure.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Skew installation concentrates local pressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b345-v16-s3","title":"彈條位移能量與橫向剪切變形","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy & Lateral shear displacement","description":"本階段聚焦「彈條位移能量」與「橫向剪切變形」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Clip elastic energy\" and \"Lateral shear displacement\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b345-v16-17","title":"彈條位移能量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「彈條位移能量」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Clip elastic energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性彈簧儲能與位移平方相關。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 J。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。無預載的線性彈簧且變形可回復；不含塑性與摩擦耗散。使用卸載回復曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「彈條位移能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Linear spring energy depends on displacement squared. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 2.2 J. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. An initially unloaded linear spring with recoverable deformation; plasticity and frictional loss are excluded. Use unloading recovery trace as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Clip elastic energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm；y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm; y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「彈條位移能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Clip elastic energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-17-k1","title":"彈條位移能量","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy","text":"線性彈簧儲能與位移平方相關。本模型把 k 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 2.2 J。","textEn":"Linear spring energy depends on displacement squared. In this model, k is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「彈條位移能量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Clip elastic energy\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","線性彈簧儲能與位移平方相關。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","Linear spring energy depends on displacement squared."],"answer":2,"explanation":"線性彈簧儲能與位移平方相關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Linear spring energy depends on displacement squared. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b345-v16-18","title":"彈條位移能量：定量估算","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「彈條位移能量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Clip elastic energy” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm；y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=2.2 J。模型邊界：無預載的線性彈簧且變形可回復；不含塑性與摩擦耗散；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm; y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 J. Boundary: An initially unloaded linear spring with recoverable deformation; plasticity and frictional loss are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以卸載回復曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型載入卸載曲線、殘餘變形及能量積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use unloading recovery trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm；y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J。只把 k 增加百分之十，y=2.2 J。模型邊界：無預載的線性彈簧且變形可回復；不含塑性與摩擦耗散；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm; y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J. Increasing only k with a ten-percent increase gives y=2.2 J. Boundary: An initially unloaded linear spring with recoverable deformation; plasticity and frictional loss are excluded; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「彈條位移能量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Clip elastic energy\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm；y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm; y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm；y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k=1000 N/mm, d=2 mm; y=0.5*k*d**2/1000=2 J. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b345-v16-19","title":"彈條位移能量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「彈條位移能量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Clip elastic energy” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以卸載回復曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型載入卸載曲線、殘餘變形及能量積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「彈條位移能量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use unloading recovery trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model loading-unloading curves, residual deformation and energy integration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clip elastic energy. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「彈條位移能量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出無預載的線性彈簧且變形可回復；不含塑性與摩擦耗散如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復造成偏離的合成觀察，以卸載回復曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clip elastic energy, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: An initially unloaded linear spring with recoverable deformation; plasticity and frictional loss are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. Explain which evidence in unloading recovery trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以卸載回復曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型載入卸載曲線、殘餘變形及能量積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「彈條位移能量」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use unloading recovery trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model loading-unloading curves, residual deformation and energy integration, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Clip elastic energy. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「彈條位移能量」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出無預載的線性彈簧且變形可回復；不含塑性與摩擦耗散如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復造成偏離的合成觀察，以卸載回復曲線說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Clip elastic energy, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: An initially unloaded linear spring with recoverable deformation; plasticity and frictional loss are excluded. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. Explain which evidence in unloading recovery trace distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「彈條位移能量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Clip elastic energy\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","本單元以卸載回復曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型載入卸載曲線、殘餘變形及能量積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Use unloading recovery trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以卸載回復曲線區分模型與觀察，先用模型載入卸載曲線、殘餘變形及能量積分建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use unloading recovery trace to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b345-v16-20","title":"彈條位移能量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Clip elastic energy: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「彈條位移能量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Clip elastic energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復。這個失效與「彈條位移能量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查卸載回復曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. This failure and a measurement bias in Clip elastic energy can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check unloading recovery trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用卸載回復曲線作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復。這個失效與「彈條位移能量」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查卸載回復曲線，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. This failure and a measurement bias in Clip elastic energy can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check unloading recovery trace rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「彈條位移能量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Clip elastic energy\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b345-v16-21","title":"橫向剪切變形：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Lateral shear displacement: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「橫向剪切變形」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Lateral shear displacement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"橫向剛度與垂向剛度是不同參數。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。使用橫向集中剛度且保持接觸；不以垂向剛度替代。使用橫向載入位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「橫向剪切變形」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Lateral and vertical stiffness are distinct parameters. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 1.65 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Lateral lumped stiffness is used with maintained contact; vertical stiffness is not substituted. Use displacement under lateral loading as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lateral shear displacement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm；y=F/k=1.5 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm; y=F/k=1.5 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「橫向剪切變形」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lateral shear displacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-21-k1","title":"橫向剪切變形","titleEn":"Lateral shear displacement","text":"橫向剛度與垂向剛度是不同參數。本模型把 F 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 1.65 mm。","textEn":"Lateral and vertical stiffness are distinct parameters. In this model, F is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「橫向剪切變形」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral shear displacement\" is correct?","options":["橫向剛度與垂向剛度是不同參數。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電"],"optionsEn":["Lateral and vertical stiffness are distinct parameters.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"橫向剛度與垂向剛度是不同參數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Lateral and vertical stiffness are distinct parameters. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b345-v16-22","title":"橫向剪切變形：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral shear displacement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「橫向剪切變形」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Lateral shear displacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm；y=F/k=1.5 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=1.65 mm。模型邊界：使用橫向集中剛度且保持接觸；不以垂向剛度替代；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm; y=F/k=1.5 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 mm. Boundary: Lateral lumped stiffness is used with maintained contact; vertical stiffness is not substituted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以橫向載入位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫向力、相對滑移與軌距方向位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use displacement under lateral loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm；y=F/k=1.5 mm。只把 F 增加百分之十，y=1.65 mm。模型邊界：使用橫向集中剛度且保持接觸；不以垂向剛度替代；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm; y=F/k=1.5 mm. Increasing only F with a ten-percent increase gives y=1.65 mm. Boundary: Lateral lumped stiffness is used with maintained contact; vertical stiffness is not substituted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「橫向剪切變形」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral shear displacement\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm；y=F/k=1.5 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm; y=F/k=1.5 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm；y=F/k=1.5 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: F=12 kN, k=8 kN/mm; y=F/k=1.5 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b345-v16-23","title":"橫向剪切變形：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral shear displacement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「橫向剪切變形」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Lateral shear displacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以橫向載入位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫向力、相對滑移與軌距方向位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橫向剪切變形」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use displacement under lateral loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model lateral force, relative slip and gauge-direction displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Lateral shear displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「橫向剪切變形」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出使用橫向集中剛度且保持接觸；不以垂向剛度替代如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化造成偏離的合成觀察，以橫向載入位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Lateral shear displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Lateral lumped stiffness is used with maintained contact; vertical stiffness is not substituted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. Explain which evidence in displacement under lateral loading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以橫向載入位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫向力、相對滑移與軌距方向位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「橫向剪切變形」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use displacement under lateral loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model lateral force, relative slip and gauge-direction displacement, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Lateral shear displacement. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「橫向剪切變形」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出使用橫向集中剛度且保持接觸；不以垂向剛度替代如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化造成偏離的合成觀察，以橫向載入位移說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Lateral shear displacement, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Lateral lumped stiffness is used with maintained contact; vertical stiffness is not substituted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. Explain which evidence in displacement under lateral loading distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「橫向剪切變形」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral shear displacement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度","本單元以橫向載入位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫向力、相對滑移與軌距方向位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","Use displacement under lateral loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以橫向載入位移區分模型與觀察，先用模型橫向力、相對滑移與軌距方向位移建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use displacement under lateral loading to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b345-v16-24","title":"橫向剪切變形：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral shear displacement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「橫向剪切變形」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lateral shear displacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化。這個失效與「橫向剪切變形」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查橫向載入位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Lateral shear displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement under lateral loading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用橫向載入位移作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化。這個失效與「橫向剪切變形」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查橫向載入位移，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. This failure and a measurement bias in Lateral shear displacement can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check displacement under lateral loading rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「橫向剪切變形」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral shear displacement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電"],"optionsEn":["Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b345-v16-s4","title":"絕緣電阻量級與溫度膨脹相容","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale & Thermal expansion compatibility","description":"本階段聚焦「絕緣電阻量級」與「溫度膨脹相容」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Insulation resistance scale\" and \"Thermal expansion compatibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b345-v16-25","title":"絕緣電阻量級：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「絕緣電阻量級」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Insulation resistance scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"低壓電阻檢查可比較濕乾狀態但不證明高壓絕緣能力。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 660 kohm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。隔離低壓直流穩態量測；結果不證明高壓耐受能力。使用同電壓下乾濕漏電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；表面污染會形成旁路導電，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕緣電阻量級」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Low-voltage resistance compares wet and dry states but does not certify high-voltage insulation. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 660 kohm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Isolated low-voltage steady DC measurement; the result does not certify high-voltage withstand. Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Insulation resistance scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=12 V, I=0.00002 A；y=V/I/1000=600 kohm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=12 V, I=0.00002 A; y=V/I/1000=600 kohm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「絕緣電阻量級」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Insulation resistance scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-25-k1","title":"絕緣電阻量級","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale","text":"低壓電阻檢查可比較濕乾狀態但不證明高壓絕緣能力。本模型把 V 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 660 kohm。","textEn":"Low-voltage resistance compares wet and dry states but does not certify high-voltage insulation. In this model, V is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「絕緣電阻量級」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Insulation resistance scale\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電","低壓電阻檢查可比較濕乾狀態但不證明高壓絕緣能力。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass.","Low-voltage resistance compares wet and dry states but does not certify high-voltage insulation.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低壓電阻檢查可比較濕乾狀態但不證明高壓絕緣能力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Low-voltage resistance compares wet and dry states but does not certify high-voltage insulation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b345-v16-26","title":"絕緣電阻量級：定量估算","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「絕緣電阻量級」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Insulation resistance scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=12 V, I=0.00002 A；y=V/I/1000=600 kohm。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=660 kohm。模型邊界：隔離低壓直流穩態量測；結果不證明高壓耐受能力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=12 V, I=0.00002 A; y=V/I/1000=600 kohm. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=660 kohm. Boundary: Isolated low-voltage steady DC measurement; the result does not certify high-voltage withstand; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以同電壓下乾濕漏電流區分模型與觀察，先用安全低壓電源、校準電流表與乾濕表面條件建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=12 V, I=0.00002 A；y=V/I/1000=600 kohm。只把 V 增加百分之十，y=660 kohm。模型邊界：隔離低壓直流穩態量測；結果不證明高壓耐受能力；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=12 V, I=0.00002 A; y=V/I/1000=600 kohm. Increasing only V with a ten-percent increase gives y=660 kohm. Boundary: Isolated low-voltage steady DC measurement; the result does not certify high-voltage withstand; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「絕緣電阻量級」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Insulation resistance scale\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=12 V, I=0.00002 A；y=V/I/1000=600 kohm。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=12 V, I=0.00002 A; y=V/I/1000=600 kohm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：V=12 V, I=0.00002 A；y=V/I/1000=600 kohm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: V=12 V, I=0.00002 A; y=V/I/1000=600 kohm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b345-v16-27","title":"絕緣電阻量級：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「絕緣電阻量級」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Insulation resistance scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以同電壓下乾濕漏電流區分模型與觀察，先用安全低壓電源、校準電流表與乾濕表面條件建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「絕緣電阻量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using safe low-voltage source, calibrated current meter and dry-wet surface conditions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Insulation resistance scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「絕緣電阻量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出隔離低壓直流穩態量測；結果不證明高壓耐受能力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由表面污染會形成旁路導電造成偏離的合成觀察，以同電壓下乾濕漏電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Insulation resistance scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Isolated low-voltage steady DC measurement; the result does not certify high-voltage withstand. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. Explain which evidence in dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：表面污染會形成旁路導電。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以同電壓下乾濕漏電流區分模型與觀察，先用安全低壓電源、校準電流表與乾濕表面條件建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「絕緣電阻量級」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using safe low-voltage source, calibrated current meter and dry-wet surface conditions, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Insulation resistance scale. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「絕緣電阻量級」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出隔離低壓直流穩態量測；結果不證明高壓耐受能力如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由表面污染會形成旁路導電造成偏離的合成觀察，以同電壓下乾濕漏電流說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Insulation resistance scale, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Isolated low-voltage steady DC measurement; the result does not certify high-voltage withstand. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. Explain which evidence in dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「絕緣電阻量級」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Insulation resistance scale\"?","options":["本單元以同電壓下乾濕漏電流區分模型與觀察，先用安全低壓電源、校準電流表與乾濕表面條件建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中"],"optionsEn":["Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以同電壓下乾濕漏電流區分模型與觀察，先用安全低壓電源、校準電流表與乾濕表面條件建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b345-v16-28","title":"絕緣電阻量級：失效診斷","titleEn":"Insulation resistance scale: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「絕緣電阻量級」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Insulation resistance scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面污染會形成旁路導電。這個失效與「絕緣電阻量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同電壓下乾濕漏電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. This failure and a measurement bias in Insulation resistance scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用同電壓下乾濕漏電流作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；表面污染會形成旁路導電，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面污染會形成旁路導電。這個失效與「絕緣電阻量級」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同電壓下乾濕漏電流，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. This failure and a measurement bias in Insulation resistance scale can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check dry and wet leakage current at equal voltage rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「絕緣電阻量級」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Insulation resistance scale\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","表面污染會形成旁路導電。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload."],"answer":1,"explanation":"表面污染會形成旁路導電。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b345-v16-29","title":"溫度膨脹相容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Thermal expansion compatibility: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「溫度膨脹相容」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Thermal expansion compatibility” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"聚合物元件熱伸長須與金屬夾持幾何一起檢查。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.396 mm。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。均勻溫升及自由聚合物伸長；約束後的預壓變化另建模。使用溫度與夾持間隙作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；熱膨脹差可能改變預壓，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溫度膨脹相容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Polymer expansion must be checked against metal-clamping geometry. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.396 mm. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Uniform heating and free polymer expansion; restrained preload changes require another model. Use temperature and clamping clearance as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Differential thermal expansion can change preload; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal expansion compatibility” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「溫度膨脹相容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal expansion compatibility”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-29-k1","title":"溫度膨脹相容","titleEn":"Thermal expansion compatibility","text":"聚合物元件熱伸長須與金屬夾持幾何一起檢查。本模型把 alpha 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.396 mm。","textEn":"Polymer expansion must be checked against metal-clamping geometry. In this model, alpha is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「溫度膨脹相容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Thermal expansion compatibility\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞","聚合物元件熱伸長須與金屬夾持幾何一起檢查。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","Polymer expansion must be checked against metal-clamping geometry."],"answer":2,"explanation":"聚合物元件熱伸長須與金屬夾持幾何一起檢查。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Polymer expansion must be checked against metal-clamping geometry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b345-v16-30","title":"溫度膨脹相容：定量估算","titleEn":"Thermal expansion compatibility: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「溫度膨脹相容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Thermal expansion compatibility” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.396 mm。模型邊界：均勻溫升及自由聚合物伸長；約束後的預壓變化另建模；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.396 mm. Boundary: Uniform heating and free polymer expansion; restrained preload changes require another model; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以溫度與夾持間隙區分模型與觀察，先用模型聚合物與金屬溫度、長度及夾持間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use temperature and clamping clearance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm。只把 alpha 增加百分之十，y=0.396 mm。模型邊界：均勻溫升及自由聚合物伸長；約束後的預壓變化另建模；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm. Increasing only alpha with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.396 mm. Boundary: Uniform heating and free polymer expansion; restrained preload changes require another model; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「溫度膨脹相容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Thermal expansion compatibility\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度"],"optionsEn":["Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K；y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: alpha=0.00008 1/K, L=150 mm, dT=30 K; y=alpha*L*dT=0.36 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b345-v16-31","title":"溫度膨脹相容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Thermal expansion compatibility: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「溫度膨脹相容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal expansion compatibility” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以溫度與夾持間隙區分模型與觀察，先用模型聚合物與金屬溫度、長度及夾持間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫度膨脹相容」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use temperature and clamping clearance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model polymer and metal temperatures, lengths and clamp clearance, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal expansion compatibility. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「溫度膨脹相容」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻溫升及自由聚合物伸長；約束後的預壓變化另建模如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由熱膨脹差可能改變預壓造成偏離的合成觀察，以溫度與夾持間隙說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal expansion compatibility, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform heating and free polymer expansion; restrained preload changes require another model. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload. Explain which evidence in temperature and clamping clearance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Differential thermal expansion can change preload. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以溫度與夾持間隙區分模型與觀察，先用模型聚合物與金屬溫度、長度及夾持間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「溫度膨脹相容」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use temperature and clamping clearance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using model polymer and metal temperatures, lengths and clamp clearance, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Thermal expansion compatibility. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「溫度膨脹相容」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出均勻溫升及自由聚合物伸長；約束後的預壓變化另建模如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由熱膨脹差可能改變預壓造成偏離的合成觀察，以溫度與夾持間隙說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Thermal expansion compatibility, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Uniform heating and free polymer expansion; restrained preload changes require another model. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload. Explain which evidence in temperature and clamping clearance distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「溫度膨脹相容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Thermal expansion compatibility\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","本單元以溫度與夾持間隙區分模型與觀察，先用模型聚合物與金屬溫度、長度及夾持間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Use temperature and clamping clearance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元以溫度與夾持間隙區分模型與觀察，先用模型聚合物與金屬溫度、長度及夾持間隙建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use temperature and clamping clearance to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b345-v16-32","title":"溫度膨脹相容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Thermal expansion compatibility: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「溫度膨脹相容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Thermal expansion compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"熱膨脹差可能改變預壓。這個失效與「溫度膨脹相容」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查溫度與夾持間隙，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Differential thermal expansion can change preload. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal expansion compatibility can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature and clamping clearance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用溫度與夾持間隙作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；熱膨脹差可能改變預壓，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Differential thermal expansion can change preload; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：熱膨脹差可能改變預壓」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Differential thermal expansion can change preload.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"熱膨脹差可能改變預壓。這個失效與「溫度膨脹相容」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查溫度與夾持間隙，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Differential thermal expansion can change preload. This failure and a measurement bias in Thermal expansion compatibility can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check temperature and clamping clearance rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「溫度膨脹相容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Thermal expansion compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞","熱膨脹差可能改變預壓。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","Differential thermal expansion can change preload."],"answer":2,"explanation":"熱膨脹差可能改變預壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Differential thermal expansion can change preload. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b345-v16-s5","title":"循環損傷指標與剛度劣化比例","titleEn":"Cycle damage index & Stiffness degradation fraction","description":"本階段聚焦「循環損傷指標」與「剛度劣化比例」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cycle damage index\" and \"Stiffness degradation fraction\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b345-v16-33","title":"循環損傷指標：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Cycle damage index: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「循環損傷指標」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Cycle damage index” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"線性累積損傷是教學近似而非普遍壽命定律。本模型把 n1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.21 1。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。各級壽命值已另給且採線性累積；忽略載入順序與交互作用。使用載重幅值分組與循環數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「循環損傷指標」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Linear damage accumulation is a teaching approximation, not a universal life law. In this model, n1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 0.21 1. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Life values for each amplitude are supplied separately and damage accumulates linearly; sequence and interaction are omitted. Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cycle damage index” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles；y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles; y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「循環損傷指標」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cycle damage index”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-33-k1","title":"循環損傷指標","titleEn":"Cycle damage index","text":"線性累積損傷是教學近似而非普遍壽命定律。本模型把 n1 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 0.21 1。","textEn":"Linear damage accumulation is a teaching approximation, not a universal life law. In this model, n1 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「循環損傷指標」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cycle damage index\" is correct?","options":["線性累積損傷是教學近似而非普遍壽命定律。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化"],"optionsEn":["Linear damage accumulation is a teaching approximation, not a universal life law.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"線性累積損傷是教學近似而非普遍壽命定律。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Linear damage accumulation is a teaching approximation, not a universal life law. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b345-v16-34","title":"循環損傷指標：定量估算","titleEn":"Cycle damage index: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「循環損傷指標」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Cycle damage index” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles；y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1。只把 n1 增加百分之十，y=0.21 1。模型邊界：各級壽命值已另給且採線性累積；忽略載入順序與交互作用；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles; y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1. Increasing only n1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.21 1. Boundary: Life values for each amplitude are supplied separately and damage accumulates linearly; sequence and interaction are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以載重幅值分組與循環數區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷幅值直方圖、循環數與各級壽命曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles；y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1。只把 n1 增加百分之十，y=0.21 1。模型邊界：各級壽命值已另給且採線性累積；忽略載入順序與交互作用；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles; y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1. Increasing only n1 with a ten-percent increase gives y=0.21 1. Boundary: Life values for each amplitude are supplied separately and damage accumulates linearly; sequence and interaction are omitted; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「循環損傷指標」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cycle damage index\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：支承不接觸時不能仍視為平行有效元件","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：偏斜安裝造成局部壓力集中"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: A support out of contact cannot remain an active parallel element.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles; y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Skew installation concentrates local pressure."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles；y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: n1=100000 cycles, N1=1000000 cycles, n2=200000 cycles, N2=2000000 cycles; y=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.2 1. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b345-v16-35","title":"循環損傷指標：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cycle damage index: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「循環損傷指標」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Cycle damage index” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以載重幅值分組與循環數區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷幅值直方圖、循環數與各級壽命曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「循環損傷指標」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic load-amplitude histogram, cycle counts and amplitude-specific life curves, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cycle damage index. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「循環損傷指標」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各級壽命值已另給且採線性累積；忽略載入順序與交互作用如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞造成偏離的合成觀察，以載重幅值分組與循環數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cycle damage index, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Life values for each amplitude are supplied separately and damage accumulates linearly; sequence and interaction are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. Explain which evidence in load-amplitude groups and cycle counts distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以載重幅值分組與循環數區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷幅值直方圖、循環數與各級壽命曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「循環損傷指標」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using synthetic load-amplitude histogram, cycle counts and amplitude-specific life curves, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Cycle damage index. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「循環損傷指標」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出各級壽命值已另給且採線性累積；忽略載入順序與交互作用如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞造成偏離的合成觀察，以載重幅值分組與循環數說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Cycle damage index, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Life values for each amplitude are supplied separately and damage accumulates linearly; sequence and interaction are omitted. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. Explain which evidence in load-amplitude groups and cycle counts distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「循環損傷指標」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cycle damage index\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：沿用垂向剛度會誤估軌距變化","本單元以載重幅值分組與循環數區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷幅值直方圖、循環數與各級壽命曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Using vertical stiffness misestimates gauge movement.","Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts to distinguish the model from observation in this unit."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以載重幅值分組與循環數區分模型與觀察，先用合成載荷幅值直方圖、循環數與各級壽命曲線建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use load-amplitude groups and cycle counts to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b345-v16-36","title":"循環損傷指標：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cycle damage index: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「循環損傷指標」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cycle damage index” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞。這個失效與「循環損傷指標」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載重幅值分組與循環數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. This failure and a measurement bias in Cycle damage index can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check load-amplitude groups and cycle counts rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用載重幅值分組與循環數作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞。這個失效與「循環損傷指標」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查載重幅值分組與循環數，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. This failure and a measurement bias in Cycle damage index can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check load-amplitude groups and cycle counts rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「循環損傷指標」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cycle damage index\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略載入順序與腐蝕會低估實際疲勞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring load sequence and corrosion understates actual fatigue. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b345-v16-37","title":"剛度劣化比例：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stiffness degradation fraction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「剛度劣化比例」如何影響軌道扣件彈性設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stiffness degradation fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Resilient rail-fastening design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"前後比較須保持溫度與載重區間一致。本模型把 k0 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.2727 percent。這個比較描述明列方程的局部敏感度，不能把相關變數也一起改變後仍稱為相同測試。前後採相同載荷區間、溫度及測試速率；初始剛度非零。使用同條件基準與複測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「剛度劣化比例」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before-after comparison requires matched temperature and loading range. In this model, k0 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed. A ten-percent increase means the output increases to 27.2727 percent. This comparison describes the sensitivity of the stated equation; changing correlated variables at the same time would be a different experiment. Before-after load interval, temperature and test rate match; initial stiffness is nonzero. Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions as measurement evidence that the equation represents the intended physical quantity. Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stiffness degradation fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm；y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm; y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent.","failure":"常見誤解：「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「剛度劣化比例」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stiffness degradation fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-37-k1","title":"剛度劣化比例","titleEn":"Stiffness degradation fraction","text":"前後比較須保持溫度與載重區間一致。本模型把 k0 當成主動改變的輸入，其餘輸入固定；當它增加百分之十，輸出增加為 27.2727 percent。","textEn":"Before-after comparison requires matched temperature and loading range. In this model, k0 is deliberately changed while every other input is held fixed.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「剛度劣化比例」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stiffness degradation fraction\" is correct?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化","前後比較須保持溫度與載重區間一致。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.","Before-after comparison requires matched temperature and loading range.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad."],"answer":1,"explanation":"前後比較須保持溫度與載重區間一致。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before-after comparison requires matched temperature and loading range. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b345-v16-38","title":"剛度劣化比例：定量估算","titleEn":"Stiffness degradation fraction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「剛度劣化比例」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stiffness degradation fraction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm；y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent。只把 k0 增加百分之十，y=27.2727 percent。模型邊界：前後採相同載荷區間、溫度及測試速率；初始剛度非零；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original assumed example, not field operating values: k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm; y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent. Increasing only k0 with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.2727 percent. Boundary: Before-after load interval, temperature and test rate match; initial stiffness is nonzero; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：本單元以同條件基準與複測區分模型與觀察，先用配對力位移曲線、試件溫度及重複測試誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm；y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent。只把 k0 增加百分之十，y=27.2727 percent。模型邊界：前後採相同載荷區間、溫度及測試速率；初始剛度非零；上式只代表本單元明列項，不把它視為完整驗證。","textEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm; y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent. Increasing only k0 with a ten-percent increase gives y=27.2727 percent. Boundary: Before-after load interval, temperature and test rate match; initial stiffness is nonzero; this equation represents only the explicitly listed term and is not a complete verification.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「剛度劣化比例」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stiffness degradation fraction\", which statement holds?","options":["本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：把串聯當平行會高估支承剛度","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：塑性變形使能量不再完全可回復","原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm；y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent。"],"optionsEn":["This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Treating series support as parallel overestimates stiffness.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Plastic deformation makes stored work partly irrecoverable.","Original assumed example, not field operating values: k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm; y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想算例，輸入不是現場操作值：k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm；y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original assumed example, not field operating values: k0=40 kN/mm, k1=32 kN/mm; y=(k0-k1)/k0*100=20 percent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b345-v16-39","title":"剛度劣化比例：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stiffness degradation fraction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「剛度劣化比例」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stiffness degradation fraction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"本單元以同條件基準與複測區分模型與觀察，先用配對力位移曲線、試件溫度及重複測試誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「剛度劣化比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired force-displacement curves, specimen temperature and repeat-test error, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Stiffness degradation fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：重算「剛度劣化比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出前後採相同載荷區間、溫度及測試速率；初始剛度非零如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化造成偏離的合成觀察，以同條件基準與複測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","observationEn":"Site practice: Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Stiffness degradation fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Before-after load interval, temperature and test rate match; initial stiffness is nonzero. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. Explain which evidence in baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","failure":"注意干擾：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"本單元以同條件基準與複測區分模型與觀察，先用配對力位移曲線、試件溫度及重複測試誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。將輸入表與輸出表分開保存，記下校正、解析度及時間戳記；至少改變一個輸入並保持其餘條件，檢查結果方向是否符合「剛度劣化比例」的方程。殘差超出事先設定的教學容差時，先查單位與量測鏈，再查省略的物理項。","textEn":"Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Establish a baseline using paired force-displacement curves, specimen temperature and repeat-test error, then repeat at the same locations and conditions. Keep input and output records separate, recording calibration, resolution and timestamps. Change one input while holding others fixed and check the trend predicted by Stiffness degradation fraction. When residuals exceed a predefined teaching tolerance, examine units and the measurement chain before attributing the difference to omitted physics.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"重算「剛度劣化比例」的基準與所列單一輸入變動案例，畫出輸入至輸出的關係，並寫出前後採相同載荷區間、溫度及測試速率；初始剛度非零如何限制結論。接著設計一組符合模型及一組由溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化造成偏離的合成觀察，以同條件基準與複測說明哪個證據能分辨兩者，保留單位及有效位數。","textEn":"Recalculate the baseline and specified single-input perturbation for Stiffness degradation fraction, plot the input-output relationship, and explain the limiting assumption: Before-after load interval, temperature and test rate match; initial stiffness is nonzero. Construct one synthetic observation consistent with the model and another affected by this failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. Explain which evidence in baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions distinguishes them, keeping units and justified significant figures throughout.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「剛度劣化比例」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stiffness degradation fraction\"?","options":["本單元以同條件基準與複測區分模型與觀察，先用配對力位移曲線、試件溫度及重複測試誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：表面污染會形成旁路導電"],"optionsEn":["Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Surface contamination creates a conductive bypass."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以同條件基準與複測區分模型與觀察，先用配對力位移曲線、試件溫度及重複測試誤差建立基準，再保留相同量測位置與工況重複比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions to distinguish the model from observation in this unit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b345-v16-40","title":"剛度劣化比例：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stiffness degradation fraction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"prerequisiteIds":["b345-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「剛度劣化比例」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stiffness degradation fraction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化。這個失效與「剛度劣化比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同條件基準與複測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. This failure and a measurement bias in Stiffness degradation fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：使用同條件基準與複測作量測證據，才能檢查方程是否對應此處的實際物理量；溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化，因此應把該原因與量測偏差分開。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing; separate that causal mechanism from bias in the measurement chain.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b345-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化。這個失效與「剛度劣化比例」的量測偏差可能產生相似表象，因此必須同時檢查同條件基準與複測，不能只靠一個合成指標判定原因。若資料無法區分兩種假說，結論應保留未確定狀態，並提出下一項可推翻假說的獨立測試。","textEn":"Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. This failure and a measurement bias in Stiffness degradation fraction can produce similar symptoms. Cross-check baseline and repeat tests under matched conditions rather than diagnosing from one aggregate score. If the available observations cannot distinguish the hypotheses, retain an unresolved conclusion and specify an independent test that could falsify one explanation. Repeating the same biased sensor is not independent confirmation.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]},{"id":"b345-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「剛度劣化比例」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stiffness degradation fraction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化。","本單元絕不可能出現這種失效：非線性墊片用單一剛度會漏掉載重依賴"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing.","This unit cannot exhibit the following failure: One stiffness misses load dependence in a nonlinear pad."],"answer":1,"explanation":"溫度軟化可能被誤認為永久老化。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Temperature softening can be mistaken for permanent ageing. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-track-fast","v16s-track-trans","v16s-track-tsi","v16s-track-fra"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b345-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b345-en.svg"}};
